99 550.2,37.744000000000014 550.9,37.365999999999985 551.6,37.016000000000005 552.3,36.694 553,36.400000000000006 553.7,36.134 554.4,35.896 555.1,35.68600000000001 555.8,35.504000000000005 556.5,35.35000000000001 557.2,35.224000000000004 557.9,35.126000000000005 558.6,35.056 559.3,35.013999999999996 560,35 560.7,35.013999999999996 561.4,35.056 562.1,35.126000000000005 562.8,35.224000000000004 563.5,35.35000000000001 564.2,35.504000000000005 564.9,35.68600000000001 565.6,35.896 566.3,36.134 567,36.400000000000006 567.7,36.694 568.4,37.016000000000005 569.1,37.365999999999985 569.8,37.744000000000014 570.5,38.14999999999999 571.2,38.584 571.9,39.04599999999999 572.6,39.536000000000016 573.3,40.054 574,40.60000000000001 574.7,41.17400000000001 575.4,41.775999999999996 576.1,42.40599999999999 576.8,43.06399999999999 577.5,43.75 578.2,44.464 578.9,45.20599999999999 579.6,45.976 580.3,46.774000000000015 581,47.60000000000001 581.7,48.45400000000001 582.4,49.335999999999984 583.1,50.245999999999995 583.8,51.18399999999998 584.5,52.150000000000006 585.2,53.14399999999999 585.9,54.166 586.6,55.21599999999998 587.3,56.29400000000001 588,57.39999999999999 588.7,58.53400000000002 589.4,59.695999999999984 590.1,60.886000000000024 590.8,62.104 591.5,63.34999999999998 592.2,64.624 592.9,65.926 593.6,67.25599999999999 594.3,68.614 595,70\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ff0000\" stroke-width=\"1\"></polyline><foreignObject x=\"497\" y=\"0\" width=\"60\" height=\"22\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math></div></foreignObject><circle cx=\"525\" cy=\"112\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#ff0000\"></circle></svg><figcaption><math><mi>f</mi></math> is continuous at <math><mi>c</mi></math>; <math><mrow><msub><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>; <math><mrow><msub><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math> does not exist.</figcaption></figure>","hidden":true,"type":"code"},{"input":"Although a function cannot have a limit at an endpoint of its domain, it can still have a one-sided limit there. We extend the definition of continuity to provide for such situations.\n\n::: definition\nWe say that ``f`` is *right continuous* at ``c`` if ``\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to c^+}f\\left(x\\right)=f\\left(c\\right)``.\n\nWe say that ``f`` is *left continuous* at ``c`` if ``\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to c^-}f\\left(x\\right)=f\\left(c\\right)``.\n:::\n\n{.aside}\n!!! example\n\n    The Heaviside function ``H\\left(x\\right)`` is continuous at every number ``x`` except ``0``. It is right continuous at ``0`` but is not left continuous or continuous there.","output":"","result":"Although a function cannot have a limit at an endpoint of its domain, it can still have a one-sided limit there. We extend the definition of continuity to provide for such situations.\n\n::: definition\nWe say that ``f`` is *right continuous* at ``c`` if ``\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to c^+}f\\left(x\\right)=f\\left(c\\right)``.\n\nWe say that ``f`` is *left continuous* at ``c`` if ``\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to c^-}f\\left(x\\right)=f\\left(c\\right)``.\n:::\n\n{.aside}\n!!! example\n\n    The Heaviside function ``H\\left(x\\right)`` is continuous at every number ``x`` except ``0``. It is right continuous at ``0`` but is not left continuous or continuous there.","resultHTML":"<p>Although a function cannot have a limit at an endpoint of its domain, it can still have a one-sided limit there. We extend the definition of continuity to provide for such situations.</p>\n<div data-type=\"definition\">\n<p>We say that <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(f\\)</span> is <em>right continuous</em> at <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(c\\)</span> if <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to c^+}f\\left(x\\right)=f\\left(c\\right)\\)</span>.</p>\n<p>We say that <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(f\\)</span> is <em>left continuous</em> at <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(c\\)</span> if <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to c^-}f\\left(x\\right)=f\\left(c\\right)\\)</span>.</p>\n</div>\n<aside data-type=\"example\">\n<p>The Heaviside function <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(H\\left(x\\right)\\)</span> is continuous at every number <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(x\\)</span> except <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(0\\)</span>. It is right continuous at <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(0\\)</span> but is not left continuous or continuous there.</p>\n</aside>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{},"translationSource":null},{"input":"const scale = 50;\nconst red = \"#ff0000\";\nconst figure = JSCells.figure({\n    width: 3 * scale,\n    height: 2 * scale,\n    caption: \"The Heaviside function\",\n});\n\nfigure.axes({\n    origin: [1.5 * scale, 1.5 * scale],\n    scale,\n    y: { ticks: [1] },\n});\n\nfigure.plot(() => 0, {\n    domain: [-1.5, 0],\n    samples: 151,\n    stroke: red,\n});\nfigure.plot(() => 1, {\n    domain: [0, 1.5],\n    samples: 151,\n    stroke: red,\n});\n\nfigure.point(0, 1, { radius: 3, fill: red, stroke: red });\nfigure.point(0, 0, { radius: 3, fill: \"#ffffff\", stroke: red });\n\nfigure.label(\"O\", {\n    x: 1.5 * scale - 16,\n    y: 1.5 * scale,\n    latex: true,\n    width: 14,\n    height: 18,\n});\n\nfigure;","output":"","result":"xy1OThe Heaviside function","resultHTML":"<figure><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"150\" height=\"100\" viewBox=\"0 0 150 100\"><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"75\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"75\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><line x1=\"75\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"75\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><polygon points=\"150,75 143,71 143,79\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"></polygon><polygon points=\"75,0 71,7 79,7\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"></polygon><foreignObject x=\"136\" y=\"45\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>x</mi></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"83\" y=\"-2\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>y</mi></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"71\" y1=\"25\" x2=\"79\" y2=\"25\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"51\" y=\"13\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mn>1</mn></math></div></foreignObject><polyline points=\"0,75 0.5,75 1,75 1.5,75 2,75 2.5,75 3,75 3.5,75 4,75 4.5,75 5,75 5.5,75 6,75 6.5,75 7,75 7.5,75 8,75 8.5,75 9,75 9.5,75 10,75 10.5,75 11,75 11.5,75 12,75 12.5,75 13,75 13.5,75 14,75 14.5,75 15,75 15.5,75 16,75 16.5,75 17.000000000000007,75 17.500000000000007,75 17.999999999999993,75 18.500000000000007,75 18.999999999999993,75 19.500000000000007,75 19.999999999999993,75 20.499999999999993,75 21,75 21.5,75 22,75 22.5,75 23,75 23.5,75 24,75 24.5,75 25,75 25.5,75 26,75 26.5,75 27,75 27.5,75 28,75 28.5,75 29,75 29.5,75 30,75 30.5,75 31,75 31.5,75 32,75 32.5,75 33,75 33.5,75 34,75 34.5,75 35,75 35.5,75 36,75 36.5,75 37,75 37.5,75 38,75 38.5,75 39,75 39.5,75 40,75 40.5,75 41,75 41.5,75 42,75 42.5,75 43,75 43.5,75 44,75 44.5,75 45,75 45.5,75 46,75 46.5,75 47,75 47.5,75 48,75 48.5,75 49,75 49.5,75 50,75 50.5,75 51,75 51.5,75 52,75 52.5,75 53,75 53.5,75 54,75 54.5,75 55,75 55.5,75 56.00000000000001,75 56.49999999999999,75 57,75 57.5,75 58,75 58.5,75 59,75 59.5,75 60,75 60.5,75 61,75 61.5,75 62,75 62.5,75 63,75 63.5,75 64,75 64.5,75 65,75 65.5,75 66,75 66.5,75 67,75 67.5,75 68,75 68.5,75 69,75 69.5,75 70,75 70.5,75 71,75 71.5,75 72,75 72.5,75 73,75 73.5,75 74,75 74.5,75 75,75\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ff0000\"></polyline><polyline points=\"75,25 75.5,25 76,25 76.5,25 77,25 77.5,25 78,25 78.5,25 79,25 79.5,25 80,25 80.5,25 81,25 81.5,25 82,25 82.5,25 83,25 83.5,25 84,25 84.5,25 85,25 85.5,25 86,25 86.5,25 87,25 87.5,25 88,25 88.5,25 89,25 89.5,25 90,25 90.5,25 91,25 91.5,25 92,25 92.5,25 93,25 93.5,25 94,25 94.5,25 95,25 95.5,25 96,25 96.5,25 97,25 97.5,25 98,25 98.5,25 99,25 99.5,25 100,25 100.5,25 101,25 101.5,25 102,25 102.5,25 103,25 103.5,25 104,25 104.5,25 105,25 105.5,25 106,25 106.5,25 107,25 107.5,25 108,25 108.5,25 109,25 109.5,25 110,25 110.5,25 111,25 111.5,25 112,25 112.5,25 113,25 113.5,25 114,25 114.5,25 115,25 115.5,25 116,25 116.5,25 117,25 117.5,25 118,25 118.5,25 119,25 119.5,25 120,25 120.5,25 121,25 121.5,25 122,25 122.5,25 123,25 123.5,25 124,25 124.5,25 125,25 125.5,25 126,25 126.5,25 127,25 127.5,25 128,25 128.5,25 129,25 129.5,25 130,25 130.5,25 131,25 131.5,25 132,25 132.5,25 133,25 133.5,25 134,25 134.5,25 135,25 135.5,25 136,25 136.5,25 137,25 137.5,25 138,25 138.5,25 139,25 139.5,25 140,25 140.5,25 141,25 141.5,25 142,25 142.5,25 143,25 143.5,25 144,25 144.5,25 145,25 145.5,25 146,25 146.5,25 147,25 147.5,25 148,25 148.5,25 149,25 149.5,25 150,25\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ff0000\"></polyline><circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"25\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#ff0000\" stroke=\"#ff0000\"></circle><circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"75\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#ff0000\"></circle><foreignObject x=\"59\" y=\"75\" width=\"14\" height=\"18\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>O</mi></math></div></foreignObject></svg><figcaption>The Heaviside function</figcaption></figure>","hidden":true,"type":"code"},{"input":"The relationship between continuity and one-sided continuity is summarized in the following theorem.\n\n::: proposition\nFunction ``f`` is continuous at ``c`` if and only if it is both right continuous and left continuous at ``c``.\n:::\n\nWe have defined the concept of continuity at a point. Of greater importance is the concept of continuity on an interval.\n\n::: definition \"Continuity of a function on an interval\"\nA function ``f`` is continuous on an interval if it is continuous at every point of that interval. In the case of an endpoint of a closed interval, ``f`` need only be continuous on one side. Thus, ``f`` is continuous on the interval ``\\left[a,b\\right]`` if\n\n```math\n\\lim_{x\\to t}f\\left(x\\right)=f\\left(t\\right)\\,\\quad\\forall t:a<t<b\\,,\n```\n\nand\n\n```math\n\\lim_{x\\to a^+}f\\left(x\\right)=f\\left(a\\right)\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad\\lim_{x\\to b^-}f\\left(x\\right)=f\\left(b\\right)\\,.\n```\n:::\n\nThese concepts are illustrated in following figure.","output":"","result":"The relationship between continuity and one-sided continuity is summarized in the following theorem.\n\n::: proposition\nFunction ``f`` is continuous at ``c`` if and only if it is both right continuous and left continuous at ``c``.\n:::\n\nWe have defined the concept of continuity at a point. Of greater importance is the concept of continuity on an interval.\n\n::: definition \"Continuity of a function on an interval\"\nA function ``f`` is continuous on an interval if it is continuous at every point of that interval. In the case of an endpoint of a closed interval, ``f`` need only be continuous on one side. Thus, ``f`` is continuous on the interval ``\\left[a,b\\right]`` if\n\n```math\n\\lim_{x\\to t}f\\left(x\\right)=f\\left(t\\right)\\,\\quad\\forall t:a<t<b\\,,\n```\n\nand\n\n```math\n\\lim_{x\\to a^+}f\\left(x\\right)=f\\left(a\\right)\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad\\lim_{x\\to b^-}f\\left(x\\right)=f\\left(b\\right)\\,.\n```\n:::\n\nThese concepts are illustrated in following figure.","resultHTML":"<p>The relationship between continuity and one-sided continuity is summarized in the following theorem.</p>\n<div data-type=\"proposition\">\n<p>Function <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(f\\)</span> is continuous at <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(c\\)</span> if and only if it is both right continuous and left continuous at <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(c\\)</span>.</p>\n</div>\n<p>We have defined the concept of continuity at a point. Of greater importance is the concept of continuity on an interval.</p>\n<div data-type=\"definition\">\n<h5>Continuity of a function on an interval</h5>\n<p>A function <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(f\\)</span> is continuous on an interval if it is continuous at every point of that interval. In the case of an endpoint of a closed interval, <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(f\\)</span> need only be continuous on one side. Thus, <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(f\\)</span> is continuous on the interval <span class=\"math-tex\" data-type=\"tex\">\\(\\left[a,b\\right]\\)</span> if</p>\n<div data-type=\"equation\" class=\"math-tex\">\n\\[\n\\lim_{x\\to t}f\\left(x\\right)=f\\left(t\\right)\\,\\quad\\forall t:a&lt;t&lt;b\\,,\n\\]\n</div>\n<p>and</p>\n<div data-type=\"equation\" class=\"math-tex\">\n\\[\n\\lim_{x\\to a^+}f\\left(x\\right)=f\\left(a\\right)\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad\\lim_{x\\to b^-}f\\left(x\\right)=f\\left(b\\right)\\,.\n\\]\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>These concepts are illustrated in following figure.</p>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{},"translationSource":null},{"input":"const scale = 80;\nconst red = \"#ff0000\";\nconst figure = JSCells.figure({\n    width: 5.5 * scale,\n    height: 2 * scale,\n    caption: \"\\\\(f\\\\) is continuous on the intervals \\\\([a,b]\\\\), \\\\(]b,c[\\\\), \\\\([c,d]\\\\), and \\\\(]d,e]\\\\).\",\n});\n\nfigure.axes({\n    origin: [0.5 * scale, 1.5 * scale],\n    scale,\n    x: {\n        ticks: [\n            { value: 0.5, label: \"a\", length: 1 },\n            { value: 1.5, label: \"b\", length: 1 },\n            { value: 2.5, label: \"c\", length: 1 },\n            { value: 3.5, label: \"d\", length: 1 },\n            { value: 4.5, label: \"e\", length: 1 },\n        ],\n    },\n});\n\nconst first = (x) => -((x - 1.25) ** 2) + 1;\nconst second = (x) => -0.5 * (x - 1.5) ** 2 + 1.25;\nconst third = (x) => x - 2.25;\nconst fourth = (x) => -0.25 * (x - 2.25) + 1;\n\nconst plot = (fn, start, end) =>\n    figure.plot(fn, { domain: [start, end], samples: 101, stroke: red });\nconst point = (x, y, fill) =>\n    figure.point(x, y, { radius: 3, fill, stroke: red });\n\nplot(first, 0.5, 1.5);\npoint(0.5, first(0.5), red);\npoint(1.5, first(1.5), red);\n\nplot(second, 1.5, 2.5);\npoint(1.5, 1.25, \"#ffffff\");\npoint(2.5, 0.75, \"#ffffff\");\n\nplot(third, 2.5, 3.5);\npoint(2.5, third(2.5), red);\npoint(3.5, third(3.5), red);\n\nplot(fourth, 3.5, 4.5);\npoint(4.5, fourth(4.5), red);\npoint(3.5, -0.25 * 1.25 + 1, \"#ffffff\");\n\nfigure.label(\"O\", {\n    x: 0.5 * scale - 16,\n    y: 1.5 * scale,\n    latex: true,\n    width: 14,\n    height: 18,\n});\n\nfigure;","output":"","result":"xyabcdeOf is continuous on the intervals [a,b], ]b,c[, [c,d], and ]d,e].","resultHTML":"<figure><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"440\" height=\"160\" viewBox=\"0 0 440 160\"><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"440\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"160\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><polygon points=\"440,120 433,116 433,124\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"></polygon><polygon points=\"40,0 36,7 44,7\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"></polygon><foreignObject x=\"426\" y=\"90\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>x</mi></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"48\" y=\"-2\" width=\"14\" height=\"28\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>y</mi></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"116\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"124\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"73\" y=\"128\" width=\"14\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>a</mi></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"160\" y1=\"116\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"124\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"153\" y=\"128\" width=\"14\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>b</mi></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"240\" y1=\"116\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"124\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"233\" y=\"128\" width=\"14\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"320\" y1=\"116\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"124\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"313\" y=\"128\" width=\"14\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>d</mi></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"400\" y1=\"116\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"124\" stroke=\"#000000\"></line><foreignObject x=\"393\" y=\"128\" width=\"14\" height=\"32\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>e</mi></math></div></foreignObject><polyline points=\"80,85 80.8,83.80799999999999 81.6,82.63199999999999 82.4,81.472 83.2,80.328 84,79.2 84.80000000000001,78.088 85.60000000000001,76.99199999999999 86.4,75.912 87.19999999999999,74.848 88,73.80000000000001 88.8,72.768 89.6,71.75200000000001 90.4,70.75200000000001 91.2,69.768 92,68.8 92.80000000000001,67.848 93.6,66.912 94.39999999999999,65.992 95.19999999999999,65.08800000000001 96,64.2 96.8,63.328 97.6,62.472 98.4,61.632 99.2,60.808 100,60 100.8,59.208 101.6,58.431999999999995 102.4,57.672 103.2,56.928 104,56.19999999999999 104.80000000000001,55.488 105.60000000000001,54.792 106.4,54.111999999999995 107.2,53.44799999999999 108,52.8 108.8,52.168000000000006 109.6,51.55199999999999 110.4,50.952 111.2,50.367999999999995 112,49.8 112.8,49.248000000000005 113.6,48.712 114.39999999999999,48.19200000000001 115.19999999999999,47.688 116,47.2 116.8,46.7